#
# Counter-example for math:LogicLoweringShape: a math:MathematicalExpression that lowers
# to a logic:Formula through math:compilesToLogicFormula but omits BOTH its
# math:denotationKind and its math:logicLoweringPreservation — the silent-promotion case
# forbidden by math:UndeclaredLogicLowering. Two sh:minCount 1 constraints fail, so
# validation MUST emit shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent (math:UndeclaredLogicLowering).
# Bound by ex:ecUndeclaredLogicLowering.
@prefix math:  <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <http://example.org/math/> .
@prefix rdfs:  <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .

# A math:SymbolReference, exactly like the conforming twin logic-lowering-declared.ttl: the
# constraint is triggered by the math:compilesToLogicFormula PREDICATE, never by a target class,
# so the concrete form changes nothing about what this fixture isolates — while the abstract
# math:MathematicalExpression base names no concrete form and would raise
# math:UnrecognizedExpressionType beside math:UndeclaredLogicLowering.
ex:promotedEq a math:SymbolReference ;
    rdfs:label "Equation silently promoted to a logic: formula without declarations"@x-gmeow-english ;
    math:hasMathematicalSymbol ex:promotedEqSymbol ;
    math:compilesToLogicFormula ex:promotedFormula .

ex:promotedEqSymbol a math:MathematicalSymbol ;
    rdfs:label "the equation, as a named symbol"@x-gmeow-english .

ex:promotedFormula a logic:Formula ;
    rdfs:label "logic: formula target of the undeclared lowering"@x-gmeow-english .
